      "dcDescription": [
        "Parchment codex written in Ge'ez in Ethiopia in the nineteenth century, containing a Psalter, and at the end, a collection of prayers to Our Lady Mary, praises and thanksgiving to the Mother of God, and notes written in Amhairc. Decorative headings and bands on ff.1r, 7r, 13c, 14r, 21r, 31v, 39r, 44r, 51v, 61r, 68v, 74r, 86v, 97v, 100v, 106r, 112r, and 123v. The manuscript has a multi-colour, striped fabric binding cover with long straps. The leather satchel is housed separate (CBL W 908.1)."
      ],
      "dcDescriptionLangAware": {
        "en": [
          "Parchment codex written in Ge'ez in Ethiopia in the nineteenth century, containing a Psalter, and at the end, a collection of prayers to Our Lady Mary, praises and thanksgiving to the Mother of God, and notes written in Amhairc. Decorative headings and bands on ff.1r, 7r, 13c, 14r, 21r, 31v, 39r, 44r, 51v, 61r, 68v, 74r, 86v, 97v, 100v, 106r, 112r, and 123v. The manuscript has a multi-colour, striped fabric binding cover with long straps. The leather satchel is housed separate (CBL W 908.1)."
        ]
